WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.810
Everyone, Kaleido Star is about to start!

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.540
When watching Kaleido Star,
please keep the room brightly lit,

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.270
and sit as far from the TV as you can.

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:14.150
Well, well, well, you get nervous
when you have to do something

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:16.050
for the first time too, don't you?

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:17.520
Thinking you have to do it right.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.490
I've just landed my first leading role.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.260
I practiced lots and did my best,

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.830
but I still got scolded for some reason.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:27.780
Oh, I just don't get it at all.
I don't. I don't.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:45.810
<i>Yaritai koto wa nani</i>

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:45.810
<i>What is it that you want to do?</i>

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.440
<i>Sou kikareru tabi</i>

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.440
<i>Every time I was asked that</i>

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:53.210
<i>Aoi sora miageta</i>

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:53.210
<i>I looked up at the blue sky</i>

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:57.190
<i>Kotae wa only my heart</i>

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:57.190
<i>The answer is only in my heart</i>

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:04.730
<i>Honto ni daiji na kotoba wa
kantan ni wa iwanai</i>

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:04.730
<i>I don't easily say the words
that are really important</i>

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:12.010
<i>Hikari ga yubisasu basho e to hashiridasu yo</i>

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:12.010
<i>I start running towards the place
the light points to</i>

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:19.980
<i>Dakishimetai mono nara
nakitai hodo mune ni aru</i>

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:19.980
<i>There's so much in my heart that I want
to embrace, I could cry</i>

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:26.920
<i>Egakitsuzukete yuku kitto
take it someday</i>

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:26.920
<i>I'll keep painting my way, I promise,
take it someday</i>

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:34.900
<i>Shiroi kumo ga nagareru
chiheisen no mukou ni</i>

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:34.900
<i>Beyond the horizon, where the white
clouds drift</i>

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:46.670
<i>Naranderu mirai wa itsumo soba ni aru kara</i>

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:46.670
<i>The future is lined up and
it'll always be there by my side</i>

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.100
This is Sora Naegino, who is playing the
role of the Little Mermaid,

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.390
and Anna Heart.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:14.340
This Kenneth Presentation is a
special two week performance,

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.370
but I hope you will enjoy the fresh new cast.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.810
Are you excited to play the lead role?

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:22.370
Please say something to Miss Layla
who is shooting a movie right now.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:27.010
Tomorrow, there's a photo shoot for
posters and a newspaper interview.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.680
And the day after tomorrow,
a photo shoot for pamphlets.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.710
Also, an appearance on cable TV
has been set.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:33.990
What?!

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.120
Oh, nothing!

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.590
I don't know, it just doesn't feel real.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.790
Pull yourself together!

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.730
Remember, you're the leading lady.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:42.860
The leading lady...

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:45.230
Facing an Amazing Wall

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:48.040
Facing an Amazing Wall

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:48.040
"Facing an Amazing Wall"

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.900
Facing an Amazing Wall

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:52.170
Sora!

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:54.080
When are you going to snap out of it?!

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:55.410
I'm sorry!

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:57.110
The photo shoot for the poster has
already started.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.170
We have to pose.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.750
Little Mermaid, let's look
a little more vibrant!

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:01.820
Oh. Yes, sir!

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.150
Prince, get a little closer
to the Little Mermaid.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:07.250
Can you set a more romantic mood?

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:11.760
Like this?

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.490
Wow...

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:15.400
Okay!

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:18.670
Anna really looked handsome.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:20.400
It made me feel really shy.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.900
I know, I know. You guys look very good.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:23.910
You think so?

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.810
What? You don't like it?

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:27.910
Personally, how I should say this?

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:28.340
I wanted it to be more like a jellyfish
waiting for his lover...

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.950
I'm sure it'll be a success!

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.950
I wanted it to be more like a jellyfish
waiting for his lover...

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.110
You think so?

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.350
I'd hope so, for their sake.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:35.110
If I were in it, it would, like,
be an absolute success.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:37.750
Don't let them get to you, Sora!

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.020
You won the part through pure talent.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.260
Don't worry, it doesn't bother me.

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:45.330
Miss Layla used to play the Little Mermaid.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:46.730
I have to do my best!

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.560
Sora!

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.270
You got a phone call!

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:54.430
A phone call?

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.540
Hello? What? Mom?

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:58.630
Yeah, that's right.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.840
It's a special presentation,

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.710
but I've been given the leading role
for the first time.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:05.980
Yeah, I'll be all right.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.240
Don't worry about me.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:09.910
Then, talk to you later.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.140
Thank you, Ken.

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.190
Was your mom happy?

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:16.490
Yeah, but she was worried about me.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:17.990
I can understand.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:18.990
This is your first leading role,

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:20.730
so I can easily see you pushing too hard.

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:22.360
Of course I'm going to be.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:24.700
I get to play the same role that
Miss Layla played,

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.170
so I have no choice but to do my best.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:29.370
Oh, Ken, did you bring that for me?

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.370
Oh, yes. Here it is.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:34.340
All right! Miss Layla's Little Mermaid!

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.310
I wanted to see this one more time!

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:38.680
With this, my performance will
just be perfect!

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:41.120
I'm also looking forward

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:41.120
Oh, I'm so happy!

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.420
to seeing your Little Mermaid.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:43.680
Thank you!

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:02.800
Miss Layla's Little Mermaid is as
wonderful as I remember it.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:04.700
She's so gorgeous and graceful.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:07.210
It's amazing.

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:09.880
The audience is so moved
and crying so much.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.950
After all, it's famous for being a show
that makes people cry.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.740
Kaleido Stage's Little Mermaid...

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.550
I wish I could perform like that too.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:19.650
Smooch!

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.160
What are you doing, Fool?!

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.460
You seem awfully giddy,

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:25.820
but can you afford such an attitude?

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:35.260
The reverse Magician.

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:38.110
The card means that if you keep
being indecisive,

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:39.230
you will lose everything...

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:40.770
Please get out of the way.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:45.440
I would like it if you would look at me
just as passionately once in a while.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:55.080
Sora! Break a leg!

00:05:58.890 --> 00:05:59.880
Finally, it's time.

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:01.900
They said opening day is sold out!

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:02.800
Really?!

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:03.970
I'm so glad.

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:07.070
I was worried nobody would show up
because it's not Miss Layla.

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:08.090
Sora.

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:10.210
I'm counting on you.

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:11.370
Oh, yes, sir!

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.860
Wow, Sora looks wonderful!

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:37.960
It's incredibly graceful.

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:42.600
I can't believe it.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.210
She's just like Miss Layla.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:45.230
Sora...

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:51.570
Sora, you're the best! The best!

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:54.230
What?

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:56.880
Cheers!

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:59.050
Wasn't Sora really great?

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:01.120
Yeah, it was a perfect performance!

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:02.410
Isn't Sora coming?

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:05.050
Oh, I wonder what happened?

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:07.160
And Miss Sarah went through all this trouble

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:09.320
to celebrate her hugely successful
opening day.

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:10.730
Oh, well.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:12.760
Let's celebrate Sora's share too!

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.590
You're always in the mood to
celebrate anyway.

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:24.530
Tomorrow, I want to touch the audience's
hearts and make them cry.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.440
Just as I expected...

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:37.150
I wonder why?

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:39.380
The audience is getting smaller compared
to opening day, isn't it?

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:42.420
We haven't made any particularly
big mistakes

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:45.360
and I think the show itself has been
perfected to a high degree.

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:47.460
By the way, where's Sora?

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.270
It's me, Sora.

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:52.000
Come in.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.160
Pardon me.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:56.770
Mr. Kenneth!

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:59.830
I'm disappointed in you.

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:03.940
At this rate, it would have been better
to reopen the show with Layla.

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:07.180
It seems I misjudged you.

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:08.520
I'm very sorry.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.820
I know I may not be as good as Miss Layla,

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.190
but I'm working hard to reach her level of...

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:18.960
You don't seem to understand
why I'm disappointed.

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:19.890
What?

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:23.060
Kalos, summon Layla back here.

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:26.760
But she is still in the middle of
shooting the movie.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:30.270
Then, have her replace Sora as the lead
as soon as she's done!

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:32.940
Please wait, Mr. Kenneth!

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:34.780
So, that's the way it'll be.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:35.940
Do you understand, Sora?

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:40.400
Sora.

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:45.080
Ken, are those the questionnaires
up to yesterday?

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:46.090
Yeah.

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:47.520
Let me see them!

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:52.490
"It was a new cast, but it was wonderful,
just like watching Miss Layla."

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:54.930
"The stage was very nice.

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:56.920
It seems this is the birth of the next
generation's Miss Layla.

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:59.400
But I would like to see

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.630
Miss Layla's Little Mermaid with the new set."

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:04.170
Nobody's written anything negative,

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:06.000
but it's all about Miss Layla.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:09.480
I don't think your Little Mermaid is bad,

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:11.840
but it doesn't move people either.

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:15.980
Is that because I'm imitating
Miss Layla's performance?

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:18.750
I played the Little Mermaid that
Miss Layla created perfectly...

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:19.220
But you are not Miss Layla.

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:19.220
I played the Little Mermaid that
Miss Layla created perfectly...

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:21.120
But you are not Miss Layla.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:26.230
If you keep being indecisive,
you will lose everything.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:29.160
Is this what he meant when he said that?

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:32.160
There's no need for two Miss Laylas...

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.300
Sora, the show's starting.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:37.240
Hurry!

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:38.540
I can't do it.

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:39.440
What?

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:43.210
Because I can't appear on stage
feeling like this.

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:46.880
I don't know how I should perform.

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:49.520
Even so, the show can't start without you.

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:51.820
GO! You're the leading lady, Sora!

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:00.750
That was unusually harsh, coming from you.

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:04.500
It's a wall every new leading cast
comes up against.

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:08.670
She'll have to really agonize over it
and I'm sure it'll be hard,

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:10.610
but if she can't overcome that wall,

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:13.340
she won't ever be able to
make a role her own.

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:19.770
What...

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:22.640
What should I do?

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:27.280
I...

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:29.890
don't know.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:48.530
Sora, let's go home.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:53.440
Let's go.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:55.010
I'm sorry.

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:58.110
I was such a mess today.

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:01.360
The audience will not buy
that kind of excuse.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:02.560
Anna!

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:05.920
The audience didn't come all this way
to see a half-baked performance.

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:08.160
As the person playing opposite you,
I will say this.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.260
I want you to perform seriously tomorrow!

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:11.790
I...

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:14.500
So, let's think about it together.

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:16.740
About YOUR Little Mermaid.

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:18.500
My little mermaid?

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:23.670
You don't seem to understand
why I'm disappointed.

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:25.350
That's right!

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:27.510
Let's make it a performance they've
never seen before!

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:29.210
they've never seen...

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:32.050
Thank you, Anna, Mia.

00:12:32.050 --> 00:12:33.450
I'll give it a try.

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:35.820
You're right.

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:38.550
Everyone watches the show as if they
were the main character.

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:40.700
If I can't understand the character,

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:42.460
there's no way the character's
feelings will get across.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:46.400
But I wonder what Sora's
Little Mermaid would be like?

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:49.600
First, you'll have to get a grasp on the
Little Mermaid's feelings.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:52.100
A mermaid's feelings...

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:54.610
Oh!

00:12:54.610 --> 00:12:55.910
Do you have an idea?

00:12:56.910 --> 00:12:58.070
Oh, Sora!

00:12:58.510 --> 00:12:59.540
Sora!

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:03.180
I'll think about it in the water.

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:04.520
After all, I'm supposed to be a mermaid!

00:13:05.190 --> 00:13:07.480
I wonder if Sora is working at it?

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:10.520
Even though this is about the only thing
I can do for her...

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:13.080
Sora?!

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:15.050
There!

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.020
There!

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:19.070
What?

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:19.470
There!

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:20.570
Oh, Ken.

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:21.730
Don't "Oh" me!

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:23.840
What are you doing, Sora?!

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:26.000
You don't have time to be so laid back
and goofing off!

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:28.640
But being a mermaid is so much fun!

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:30.850
It's very beautiful in the ocean

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:33.380
and you get to swim around it all day long.

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:35.380
And there's no intensive training either.

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:36.520
She's got a point.

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:39.290
And there's nobody who's mean to you
or yells at you.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.390
That's not the issue here!

00:13:41.390 --> 00:13:43.890
I think a girl who grew up like that

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:48.630
would probably be a cheerful, spirited,
and genuine girl.

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:51.470
But the Little Mermaid is supposed to be
a tragic heroine.

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:53.270
Are you sure she should be a girl like that?

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:54.970
Thinking isn't going to get me anywhere,

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:56.700
so I'm just going to give it a try.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:08.940
Oh, really.

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:12.450
This is the first time I've seen the
Little Mermaid make people laugh.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:16.420
Maybe she finally lost her mind from the
pressure of being the lead.

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:18.020
It's way weird.

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:27.740
Thank you very much.

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:28.740
Please be careful on your way home.

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:30.370
Thank you very much.

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:31.870
What? Sora!

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:34.440
Excuse me, what did you think of
today's Little Mermaid?

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:35.210
What?

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:37.680
Well, I'd like to get your honest opinion.

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:38.980
Wait, Sora!

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:42.180
I thought she was a kind of energetic
and cute Little Mermaid, but...

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:45.020
It didn't tie in with the part when she
turned into bubbles at the end,

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:46.820
so I guess it felt a little incoherent.

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:47.860
I agree.

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:49.020
I think if it were Miss Layla,

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:52.290
I'm sure she would have been a more
graceful and refined Little Mermaid.

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:54.590
Please excuse us. Thank you very much.

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:59.200
Hey, what are you thinking, asking the
audience questions?!

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:01.400
Because I won't know unless I ask them

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:03.970
and I'll only get more confused if
I just think on my own.

00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:05.110
That doesn't mean you should...

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:07.240
But it was a bit of an improvement, right?

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:09.640
My Little Mermaid was different
from Miss Layla's.

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:14.250
Well, I suppose your personality
is showing through more...

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:15.220
Right?!

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:17.220
I also prefer the way you are now...

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:18.410
Excuse me!

00:15:19.420 --> 00:15:21.290
What was with your performance today?!

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:23.060
Whoever heard of a Little Mermaid like that?!

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:24.760
It becomes a problem for us

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:26.030
when you suddenly decide
to change your performance!

00:15:26.030 --> 00:15:28.830
Besides, you never got permission
from the production department!

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:29.900
I'm sorry.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:33.230
But I wanted to play a different
Little Mermaid than Miss Layla's.

00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:35.140
You don't have to do something like that!

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:36.770
This show is only two weeks long!

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:39.040
Anyway, please don't confuse us!

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.370
Sora...

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:49.220
I'm sorry, we got carried away too.

00:15:49.220 --> 00:15:51.420
We ended up throwing the production
into confusion...

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:54.820
No, it's not your fault. I'm the one...

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:56.590
You're not wrong, Sora.

00:15:56.590 --> 00:15:59.860
It's just that no one understands
your Little Mermaid yet.

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:00.760
Ken...

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:03.430
The run of the show has just started.

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:06.530
Once you perfect a performance
that can convince everyone...

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:08.840
You're right.

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:10.500
It's not "only two weeks".

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:12.560
We have two "whole" weeks.

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:14.310
Rather than doing it halfway,

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:17.010
I'll take the plunge and create
my very own Little Mermaid!

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:18.170
Sora...

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:25.210
Hey, what is this?

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:30.020
Oh, I'm going to live like the
Little Mermaid during the production.

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:31.190
What?

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:33.330
I'm not Miss Layla,

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:35.530
so I can't produce a calculated
performance like she does.

00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:39.630
That's why I've decided to find my role
with my own mind and body.

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:44.210
Sora!

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:45.470
Sora, are you okay?!

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:47.680
Sora, don't you think you're going too far?

00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:51.040
Your feet are probably numb from
wearing fins all the time.

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:53.050
That's right!

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:55.680
She's been swimming all her life!

00:16:55.680 --> 00:16:57.120
If she suddenly grew legs,

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.520
even the Little Mermaid might have tripped!

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:11.070
I thought a lot about the Little
Mermaid's feelings,

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:12.530
but I still don't get it.

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:13.830
Like what, for example?

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:17.100
Well, the Little Mermaid
loves the prince and that's why

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:20.140
she went so far as to exchange her voice
to become a human, right?

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:23.480
But even though the prince thinks the
wrong person saved him,

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:25.010
she doesn't say anything.

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:26.750
But she can't talk.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:27.950
She can't help it.

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:29.320
Is it really something she can't help?

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:31.050
Don't you think there might be other ways?

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:36.990
If I were her, I couldn't give up
someone I seriously love that easily.

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:39.020
But how could she...

00:17:39.790 --> 00:17:42.560
Hey, let's get everyone else's opinions too.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:47.070
Why does the Little Mermaid have to
give up her love?

00:17:47.070 --> 00:17:47.940
Yes.

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:49.740
Being unable to express herself
through words

00:17:49.740 --> 00:17:52.270
is something we have to deal with
on stage as well.

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:55.640
Yet, we can still express ourselves
by using our bodies.

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:57.780
Now that you mention it,

00:17:57.780 --> 00:18:00.750
I'd never thought about anything
outside of the script.

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:03.220
Certainly, for a modern-day audience,

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:07.190
a Little Mermaid who quietly withdraws
herself might not be satisfying.

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:08.820
Then what if she tries really hard

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:11.830
to tell him that she was the one
who saved him?

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:14.300
Maybe she'll even duel the princess
from the neighboring kingdom.

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:15.730
That might be a good idea!

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:17.700
But even then, the prince
still doesn't remember her.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:19.500
Then, what would the Little Mermaid do?

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:23.040
Take the prince's hand and jump
into the water together!

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:25.340
You mean, the prince will also
jump into the waterfall?!

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:26.640
I'll do it!

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:28.780
Anna, that's wonderful!

00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:31.080
The two of them will fall down the
waterfall, holding each other.

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:34.340
During that fall, the prince will
remember the Little Mermaid and...

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:36.420
A happy ending!

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:39.220
The Little Mermaid has a strong
tragic image, but...

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:42.820
In the end, I like happy endings
better than tragedies!

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:45.630
It sounds like this might turn into
an interesting show.

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:47.460
Then why don't we get Kalos' permission,

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:49.860
and take the plunge to change the play?

00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:10.220
It's me.

00:19:10.220 --> 00:19:11.240
Come in.

00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:16.990
I finished the film shoot early.

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:19.850
Since Mr. Kenneth contacted me.

00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:23.400
First, she completely imitates
my performance,

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:25.960
and now she's come up with an
outrageous Little Mermaid?

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:29.700
I guess playing the lead role was
still too much for her.

00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:31.510
Well, have a look at it for me.

00:19:31.510 --> 00:19:32.470
What?

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:35.040
With this kind of attendance,

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:37.440
no wonder Mr. Kenneth is complaining.

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:39.950
Kalos?

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:45.890
What is this?

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:47.760
The Little Mermaid is testing the sea witch

00:19:47.760 --> 00:19:50.490
to see if the sea witch can really use magic.

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:54.260
Why?

00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:57.160
Because the sea witch could be a liar.

00:19:57.160 --> 00:19:58.870
That's just absurd...

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:00.800
Never mind, just watch it through to the end.

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:04.940
The blue ribbon represents waves?

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:08.510
She's trying to make the prince
remember her?

00:20:12.050 --> 00:20:13.950
A Little Mermaid like that is...

00:21:04.100 --> 00:21:06.200
This is it! This is it!

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:08.500
What I wanted was a new kind of Kaleido Star

00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:10.730
that we'd never seen before!

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:19.410
Wasn't that Little Mermaid cute?

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:21.420
Yeah, it was so much fun!

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:24.580
I never realized the Little Mermaid was
such a fun story.

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:26.420
Good work!

00:21:26.420 --> 00:21:27.890
It was so fun!

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:30.360
Somehow, I was able to really
enjoy performing.

00:21:30.360 --> 00:21:31.430
Me too.

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:31.830
Sora...

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:32.790
Good work!

00:21:32.790 --> 00:21:36.660
Sora, I've got a little idea for the
ballroom scene.

00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:37.500
Okay!

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:40.130
I wonder what I should transform the
starfish into tomorrow?

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:43.040
That Little Mermaid is definitely
Sora's own creation.

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:44.100
Somewhere along the way,

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:45.900
she's become the leading performer
and the troupe leader.

00:21:46.270 --> 00:21:48.540
She's an amazing girl.

00:21:56.680 --> 00:21:58.250
In Sora's Little Mermaid,

00:21:58.250 --> 00:22:00.580
even the supporting cast were lively.

00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:04.020
Because they were given unconventional
new characters to play.

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:07.920
It looks like we have a new title
added to Kaleido Stage.

00:22:08.400 --> 00:22:11.190
The Little Mermaid that paves her own way.

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:24.550
<i>When you sabishii toki doushitemasuka</i>

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:24.550
<i>When you're lonely, what do you do?</i>

00:22:24.550 --> 00:22:26.980
<i>Never say sonna no wakannai</i>

00:22:24.550 --> 00:22:26.980
<i>Never say you don't get any of that</i>

00:22:26.980 --> 00:22:29.850
<i>Nemuru asobu magazine mekuru</i>

00:22:26.980 --> 00:22:29.850
<i>Sleep, play, flip through a magazine</i>

00:22:29.850 --> 00:22:32.190
<i>Sabishii toki wa sabishii yo</i>

00:22:29.850 --> 00:22:32.190
<i>When you're lonely, you're lonely</i>

00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:36.960
<i>Mienai denpa ga kyou mo
tulututu machi ni tobikau</i>

00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:36.960
<i>Like always, invisible vibes fly around
the city today, tulututu</i>

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:41.630
<i>Anyway kokoro no bekutoru
so many reason hanashiteru</i>

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:41.630
<i>Anyway, the vector of my heart is
talking about so many reasons</i>

00:22:41.630 --> 00:22:46.300
<i>Jiyuu ni sora o tobitai keredo</i>

00:22:41.630 --> 00:22:46.300
<i>I want to be free and fly the skies</i>

00:22:46.300 --> 00:22:51.000
<i>Hane o hirogeru basho ga nai</i>

00:22:46.300 --> 00:22:51.000
<i>But I don't have space to spread my wings</i>

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:53.170
<i>Demo shinjiteru</i>

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:53.170
<i>But I have faith</i>

00:22:53.170 --> 00:22:57.850
<i>Katachi no nai mirai ga aru yo</i>

00:22:53.170 --> 00:22:57.850
<i>There is a future yet to be shaped</i>

00:22:57.850 --> 00:23:02.520
<i>Katachi ni shitai watashi ga iru</i>

00:22:57.850 --> 00:23:02.520
<i>And there's a me that I want to shape</i>

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:09.020
<i>Kanashikutemo machigai demo</i>

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:09.020
<i>Even if I'm sad, even if it's a mistake</i>

00:23:09.020 --> 00:23:14.360
<i>Omou mama fly to the free</i>

00:23:09.020 --> 00:23:14.360
<i>I'll do what I want and
fly towards the freedom</i>

00:23:20.270 --> 00:23:22.200
Next Kaleido Star

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:24.300
Junk Baron, huh?

00:23:24.300 --> 00:23:25.940
That's a perfect stage name for me.

00:23:25.940 --> 00:23:29.340
And so, it turns out Anna's father
is a comedian.

00:23:29.340 --> 00:23:31.680
So, we all went to see his show, but...

00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:33.480
That person is not my dad!

00:23:33.480 --> 00:23:35.020
Meeting her father for
the first time in 10 years,

00:23:35.020 --> 00:23:36.480
he'd completely changed.

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:39.050
I don't want their precious memories ruined!

00:23:39.050 --> 00:23:40.420
I don't! I don't!

00:23:40.420 --> 00:23:42.890
Next time on Kaleido Star, "Anna's

00:23:42.890 --> 00:23:43.020
Not So Amazing

00:23:43.020 --> 00:23:43.920
Anna's Not So Amazing Father

00:23:43.020 --> 00:23:43.920
Not So Amazing

00:23:43.920 --> 00:23:45.160
Anna's Not So Amazing Father

00:23:43.920 --> 00:23:45.160
Father"

00:23:45.160 --> 00:23:47.030
Anna's Not So Amazing Father

00:23:45.160 --> 00:23:47.030
My wings are my dream
and on towards the sky...

00:23:47.030 --> 00:23:47.790
Anna's Not So Amazing Father
